# 🔧 AI-Assisted Development Methodology

I use AI as a reasoning and problem-solving partner, not as a blind code-generation tool.

During my transition into data science and applied AI, I developed a review-based, human-in-control workflow using ChatGPT to support planning, understanding, and systematic debugging across my projects.

## 🧠 How I Work

### 1. Problem Exploration & Design

I begin by clarifying requirements, constraints, and assumptions in natural language. ChatGPT is used to explore approaches, compare alternatives, and translate domain knowledge into a concrete plan before writing code.

### 2. Controlled Implementation

All code is written and integrated incrementally:

- AI suggestions are reviewed, adapted, and manually applied
- No automatic or inline overwrites of working code
- Design intent is preserved throughout implementation

### 3. Iterative Debugging & Learning

When issues arise, I use ChatGPT to:

- Diagnose root causes
- Understand why failures occur
- Apply targeted fixes rather than full rewrites
- Multiple refinement cycles are treated as part of the development process, not as errors

## 🛡️ Why This Approach

Inline autocompletion tools can be effective in mature codebases, but during learning and early prototyping they can:

- Introduce uncontrolled changes
- Reduce visibility into logic
- Break working systems silently

A review-first ChatGPT workflow ensures:

- Explainability over speed
- Safer iteration
- Deeper understanding of the codebase
- This mirrors scientific and analytical problem-solving practices

## 🚀 Outcomes

This methodology has enabled me to:

- Deliver complete, working data and AI projects
- Develop strong debugging and recovery skills
- Clearly articulate design decisions and trade-offs
- Use AI responsibly as a collaborator, not a crutch

The projects in this repository reflect both functional results and robust development thinking.